---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Feature from '../components/Feature.astro';
import { projects } from '../data/work';

const selected = projects.filter((p) => p.home).sort((a, b) => a.home! - b.home!);
---
<Base>
  <section class="wrap hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <h1 id="hero-title">I design interfaces, then build them all the way down.</h1>
    <p class="intro">I’m Isaac Adelore, a frontend-focused fullstack engineer who also designs. For six years I’ve built products across banking, communication and real-time software, from the Figma file to the database. The interface is where I’m strongest.</p>
    <dl class="facts">
      <div><dt>Based in</dt><dd>Lagos, Nigeria</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Works across</dt><dd>Product design, frontend architecture, APIs and data</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn solid" href="mailto:adeloreisaac@gmail.com">Email me</a>
      <a class="btn" href="https://linkedin.com/in/adeloreisaac">LinkedIn</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="about-title">About</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <div>
        <p>I started as a designer who could code and became an engineer who still designs. That means I can sit with a product team on Monday deciding what a screen should do, and be in the API on Thursday making sure it can.</p>
        <p>A clean interface that works properly is the part of the job I enjoy most. Software people depend on to get their work done is the part that keeps me at it. Most of what I’ve built is the second kind: tools a service desk, a data team or a finance lead opens every morning.</p>
        <p>I care about the details people only notice when they’re wrong: what a price change looks like, what an empty screen says, what happens when a request lands on the wrong server, and how a layout holds up on a cheap phone.</p>
      </div>
      <aside>
        <h3>Frontend</h3>
        <p>React, Next.js, Vue, Nuxt, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, TanStack Query, Zustand, Pinia</p>
        <h3>Backend and data</h3>
        <p>Laravel, ColdFusion (CFML), FastAPI, Node, SQL Server, PostgreSQL</p>
        <h3>Design</h3>
        <p>Figma, design systems, UX audits, prototyping</p>
        <h3>Education</h3>
        <p>B.Sc. Computer Science, Covenant University</p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section" id="work" aria-labelledby="work-title">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="work-title">Selected work</h2>
      <p>Web apps and marketing sites, designed and built. Internal tools are written up in full, because I can’t show their screens.</p>
    </div>
    {selected.map((p, i) => <Feature p={p} eager={i === 0} />)}
    <p class="see-all"><a class="btn" href="/work/">See all work</a></p>
  </section>
</Base>
